  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "Coagulating value of the electrolytes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> tor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>As</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>09</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn></math> respectively. The coagulating power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> times the coagulating power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "556",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The coagulating power of an electrolyte is a measure of its ability to cause the coagulation or precipitation of a colloidal solution.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Coagulation</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>power</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Coagulation</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>value</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;Coagulating value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>As</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>09</mn></math><br />&nbsp;Coagulating value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>As</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn></math></p><p>Then,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>NaCl</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>NaCl</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>09</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>NaCl</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>556</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>NaCl</mi></msub></math><br />&nbsp; So the answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>556</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p></blockquote>",
